WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.902
<v Examiner>Patterns of inheritance.

2
00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.586
<v Examiner>Four marks.

3
00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:09.525
<v Examiner>Briefly explain these patterns of inheritance, with an example of each: codominance,

4
00:00:09.525 --> 00:00:14.425
<v Examiner>incomplete dominance, polygenic inheritance, and mitochondrial inheritance.

5
00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:18.337
Four patterns, four marks, and an example for each.

6
00:00:18.337 --> 00:00:22.138
Her 2023 revision deck puts them in a four-column table,

7
00:00:22.138 --> 00:00:24.582
and that's the shape to write it in.

8
00:00:25.032 --> 00:00:27.107
The hook: co means both show.

9
00:00:27.107 --> 00:00:28.896
Incomplete means a blend.

10
00:00:28.896 --> 00:00:30.470
Poly means many genes.

11
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.901
Mito means mum only.

12
00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:33.221
Codominance.

13
00:00:33.221 --> 00:00:39.166
Both alleles are fully expressed in the heterozygote, each making its own protein.

14
00:00:39.166 --> 00:00:44.603
The example is the A B O blood groups: I A and I B together give group A B,

15
00:00:44.603 --> 00:00:48.373
with both the A and the B antigens on the red cells.

16
00:00:48.823 --> 00:00:50.155
Incomplete dominance.

17
00:00:50.155 --> 00:00:55.866
One allele doesn't completely mask the other, so the heterozygote is somewhere in between.

18
00:00:55.866 --> 00:00:57.579
Her example is sickle cell.

19
00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:01.196
The heterozygote has both normal and sickle-shaped cells,

20
00:01:01.196 --> 00:01:06.209
with about a third of the haemoglobin abnormal, and more resistance to malaria.

21
00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:09.123
Polygenic inheritance.

22
00:01:09.123 --> 00:01:14.044
Many genes control one trait, so you get a continuous range, a bell curve,

23
00:01:14.044 --> 00:01:15.907
rather than neat categories.

24
00:01:15.907 --> 00:01:18.966
Examples: height, skin colour, and eye colour.

25
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:21.091
Mitochondrial inheritance.

26
00:01:21.091 --> 00:01:26.761
The genes in mitochondrial DNA are passed on only by the mother, to all of her children,

27
00:01:26.761 --> 00:01:27.986
sons and daughters.

28
00:01:27.986 --> 00:01:29.596
Fathers never pass it on.

29
00:01:29.596 --> 00:01:33.656
These disorders can turn up in both sexes, in every generation,

30
00:01:33.656 --> 00:01:37.844
but how severe they are varies, because of the bottleneck effect:

31
00:01:37.844 --> 00:01:42.676
symptoms only appear once the mutated mitochondrial DNA passes a threshold,

32
00:01:42.676 --> 00:01:44.674
often sixty to ninety per cent.

33
00:01:44.674 --> 00:01:47.960
One example is LHON, which damages the optic nerve.

34
00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.067
The traps.

35
00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:54.796
Codominance and incomplete dominance are the pair she uses to catch you.

36
00:01:54.796 --> 00:01:57.949
Codominance: both shown in full, like A B blood.

37
00:01:57.949 --> 00:01:59.262
Incomplete: a blend.

38
00:01:59.262 --> 00:02:04.648
Second: her decks put sickle cell under incomplete dominance, so write it her way.

39
00:02:04.648 --> 00:02:08.786
Third: mitochondrial means from the mother to all her children.

40
00:02:08.786 --> 00:02:10.231
Never from the father.

41
00:02:10.681 --> 00:02:11.260
<v Examiner>Once more.

42
00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.303
<v Examiner>The four patterns.

43
00:02:14.753 --> 00:02:18.410
Codominance: both alleles are fully expressed, like A B blood,

44
00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.887
where I A and I B together give group A B.

45
00:02:20.887 --> 00:02:24.544
Incomplete dominance: one allele doesn't fully mask the other,

46
00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.549
so the heterozygote is in between,

47
00:02:26.549 --> 00:02:30.088
like sickle cell carriers with both normal and sickle cells.

48
00:02:30.088 --> 00:02:34.040
Polygenic: many genes control one trait, giving a continuous range,

49
00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.692
like height and skin colour.

50
00:02:35.692 --> 00:02:40.469
Mitochondrial: mitochondrial DNA comes only from the mother, to all her children,

51
00:02:40.469 --> 00:02:43.595
and severity varies because of the bottleneck effect.
